# T3Planet client & documentation behavior

## Audience

Readers are **TYPO3 integrators and T3Planet customers** with backend experience. Do not write beginner “open the module / page tree” steps unless the page is explicitly introductory.

Omit or remove sections like “How to open it” with generic backend navigation when the user says customers have TYPO3 knowledge.

## Voice & content craft

- Accurate, concise, no filler, no slogan/tagline lines (client rejects e.g. “A scan reports findings. Fix Hub is where work happens.”).
- Prefer concrete remediation wording: findings → continue in Fix Hub.
- Customer-facing names: **AI Foundation**, **AI Accessibility** (extension keys in backticks when helpful).
- Supademo + short explanation often beats a duplicate full UI screenshot; add screenshots when the user attaches one for a major tool (e.g. Color contrast checker).
- Complete frontmatter `description` strings — never truncate mid-word.
- Important notes: do not mix license and AI-provider requirements if the client says that misleads; put provider needs in feature/setup prose.
- Match the product: no “Choose Desktop or Mobile” if scans cover both; Fix Hub = Scanner issues only (not Lighthouse).
- CLI for integrators: document **Composer** and **Non-Composer** commands.
- Info pages (Human Expert): explanation + tables OK; skip redundant Steps.

## Local vs live

- Edits default to **local workspace** only.
- LAN preview: `http://<LAN-IP>:3000/` (fast proxy). Purge: `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:3000/__t3_cache_purge`.
- **Live** is https://docs.t3planet.de/en/latest after Mintlify deploy from **`nitsan-technologies/T3Planet-docs`** (`git push origin HEAD:master`, author **Markus**).
- Do **not** use the Markus fork as the normal deploy remote. Emergency sync to the fork only if Mintlify Git is still on the fork and live is blocked (see `mintlify-deployment.mdc`).
- Tell the user clearly whether a fix is local-only or verified on live.

## Typical user requests

| Request | Action |
|---------|--------|
| Remove / rewrite one sentence | Surgical edit + cache purge; local-only unless deploy asked |
| Remove screenshot on a live URL | Edit matching `.md`; keep Supademos unless asked to remove |
| Fix missing Card icon | Valid Lucide names (`sliders-horizontal`, `type` — not `sliders`, `text`) |
| Fix code block UI | Replace RST `::` / `code-block` with fenced `bash` / `json` |
| Content tab / card list | 1–2 lines per card + link to related Feature Guide page |
| Deploy / push / live | Markus commit → push `origin` only → verify Activity + live content |
| Train / improve context | Update `context.md` + this rule |

## Release discipline

- `mintlify validate` on Node 20 before push.
- Do not commit `RST Format */` or `scripts/remigration/*` QA artifacts unless asked.
- After nav/page changes: `python3 scripts/compute_doc_stats.py`.
- Full runbook: repo root `context.md`.

## TonicTypes product docs (2026-09-23)

- Live/product path: **`TonicTypes/`** (not `ExtTypoTonic/`).
- Professional page: **`TonicTypes/Professional/`** (not `TypoTonicProfessional`).
- Old `/ExtTypoTonic/*` URLs must keep **redirects** in `docs.json` to `/TonicTypes/*`.
- This doc set **leads with EXT:tonictypes_pro** (`k3n/tonictypes_pro`); Core (`k3n/tonictypes`) is required dependency, not the primary product framing.
- After path renames: update `docs.json` nav, hub links (`AllExtensions`), internal `/en/latest/...` hrefs, then `python3 scripts/compute_doc_stats.py` + `mintlify validate`.
